                        "content": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "**Create collective**\n\nCreate collective **Projetos 1** with a new team owned by you.\n\n- Collectives creates a new team with you as its owner and only member, and marks it as managed by Collectives, using an internal privilege of Teams, as it does in the browser.\n- Collectives creates the folder of the collective with a welcome page, Readme.md, in your language.\n- Nobody else is added, invited or sent an email.\n- If another team, even one you cannot see, already uses this display name, Teams adds “ (2)” to it.\n- On this server Teams may also create a team folder for the new team, depending on how the administrator set up team folders.\n- If, between this confirmation and the creation, a team called “Projetos 1” appears that you administer, Collectives creates the collective for that team instead: its current members get access to the collective and the team becomes managed by Collectives. The name is checked again right before.\n- If the creation fails halfway, it may not be possible to tell whether an existing team was used.\n\nNothing was changed. Confirm to execute.\n\n*Show this plan to the user and repeat the same call with confirm: true and the plan\\_state only after they agree.*\n\n*To confirm, repeat the call with plan_state `<plan_state#1>`.*"
                            }
                        ],
